label Has_met_overworker
join bartender left
bartender: Ahh, back already, friend. How was your little visit to room 101?
main_player: I talked to Richard.
bartender: Did you now? And how did you find him?
main_player: He seems pretty obsessed with his work.
bartender: Hah! That's Richard for you. The man could probably work himself into an early grave.
main_player: Doesn't anyone try to help him?
bartender: Oh, plenty have tried. Whether they actually helped is another question.”
main_player: What do you mean?
bartender: Well, everyone has their own way of dealing with things, friend. You can't simply expect people to change because you tell them to.
main_player: So what am I supposed to do?
bartender: That's for you to figure out. I'm merely the bartender, after all.
This is the end of the demo. Feel free to look around, or press ESC and then the Quit button to exit the game. Thanks for testing.
[end_timeline]
label Introduction_bartender
join bartender left
bartender: This is Lethe's End, friend. I'm the owner, and bartender, of this inn. And you are a resident, staying here for an indefinite amount of time.
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
main_player: Where am I?
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: Somewhere between where you were and where you're supposed to be.
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
main_player: Somewhere between?
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: Let's just say this is a place where people end up when they have a few things left to figure out.
bartender: You better make yourself at home, friend, because you are not leaving anytime soon, I'm afraid.
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
main_player: I don't remember anything.
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: Perhaps that's for the best, friend. Sometimes a clean slate is exactly what a person needs.
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
main_player: Why can't I remember?
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: After all, just because you have amnesia doesn't mean you have no culpability.
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
main_player: What does that mean?
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: This is just my word, but maybe you deserve it?
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
You become concerned about your situation, whilst the bartender remains calm and dismissive.
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: Now now, relax, there is no reason to have an elevated heartbeat in this instance...
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
main_player: How do I get out?
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: Don't bother asking for the exit. This is purgatory\: the whole concept doesn't support haphazard departures.
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
main_player: What am I supposed to do?
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: Well, find a way to convince him to leave his room.
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
When you ask about the residents, the bartender gives just enough information to point them in the right direction.
main_player: Who is resident 101?
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: Ahh, resident 101. Richard. 'The Overworker' I call him.
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
main_player: Why?
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: You should see for yourself, then you'd understand.
leave bartender [animation="Instant Out"]
The bartender can also provide access to parts of the mansion when the player needs it, but always keeps his own detached attitude.
main_player: I guess i'll go see this 'Overworker' person, then.
join bartender left [animation="Instant In"]
bartender: Good luck, friend.
leave bartender [animation="Fade Out" length="1.0"]
set {bartender.HasMetBartender} = true
[end_timeline]
label Has_not_met_overworker
if randf() < 0.33:
	bartender: Have you talked to Richard yet?
elif randf() < 0.66:
	bartender: He should be upstairs in room 101.
else:
	bartender: Go check on the Overworker first.
[end_timeline]